{"NoopCache used for in-proc AuthZ client disables client-side caching, defeating caching benefits and potentially causing higher DB load and latency for repeated checks in high-traffic environments": 0.46203309297561646, "Potential data race when reading permission cache maps - the code stores per-user permissions as map[string]bool and returns that map directly to callers, which can cause race conditions if another goroutine updates the same cache entry concurrently": 0.20226892828941345, "Denial cache needs comprehensive test coverage for all code paths: denial cache hit short-circuits, denial cache TTL semantics, and scenario where denial cache misses but permission is later denied": 0.171297088265419, "getUserPermissions uses singleflight.Do and returns res.(map[string]bool) type assertion which could panic if Do returns nil or different type due to unexpected path": 0.11547146737575531, "Tests rely on internal cache semantics and need additional coverage for edge cases like concurrent cache refresh, cache eviction boundaries, and cross-identity-type caching coherency": 0.03276178985834122, "Hard to audit token-exchange / in-proc server interaction with potential for token leakage if in-proc interceptor is misconfigured": 0.0064759948290884495, "CHANGELOG.md not updated to describe new authz caching features (NoopCache, denial cache, getCachedIdentityPermissions, shadow-proxy)": 0.0291447751224041, "High commit churn with multiple merge commits raises risk of subtle regressions and conflicts in RBAC/cache paths": 0.003399271983653307, "No explicit CONTRIBUTING.md file observed - should confirm it covers new authz caching changes and testing guidelines": 0.01799071580171585}